{"id":"mahabharata-6-108","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":108,"title":"अष्टाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 108 · Tenth day: ill omens and Bhishma's blaze","summary":{"en":"Bhishma drives back the Pandava chariots like a rutting elephant, and the sacred images in the temples shake and weep. Sanjaya speaks of evil omens, and Bhishma burns the great host like a god of death.","kn":"ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಮದಗಜದಂತೆ ಪಾಂಡವ ರಥಗಳನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದೇವಾಲಯಗಳಲ್ಲಿನ ವಿಗ್ರಹಗಳು ನಡುಗಿ ಅಳುತ್ತವೆ. ಸಂಜಯ ಅಪಶಕುನಗಳನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಯಮನಂತೆ ಮಹಾಸೇನೆಯನ್ನು ಸುಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म मतवाले हाथी की तरह पाण्डव रथों को भगाते हैं, और मन्दिरों की मूर्तियाँ काँपती और रोती हैं। संजय अपशकुनों की बात करते हैं, और भीष्म यम की तरह विशाल सेना को जलाते हैं।","te":"భీష్ముడు మదగజంలా పాండవ రథాలను తరుముతాడు; ఆలయాల్లోని దేవతా విగ్రహాలు వణికి ఏడుస్తాయి. సంజయుడు దుశ్శకునాలను చెబుతాడు; భీష్ముడు యముని వలె మహాసేనను దహిస్తాడు.","ta":"பீஷ்மர் மதயானை போல் பாண்டவத் தேர்களை விரட்டுகிறார்; கோயில்களிலுள்ள தெய்வச் சிலைகள் நடுங்கி அழுகின்றன. சஞ்சயன் துர்நிமித்தங்களைக் கூற, பீஷ்மர் யமன் போல் பெரும்படையை எரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"മദയാനയെപ്പോലെ ഭീഷ്മർ പാണ്ഡവ രഥങ്ങളെ പിന്നോട്ടോടിക്കുന്നു; ക്ഷേത്രങ്ങളിലെ പുണ്യബിംബങ്ങൾ കുലുങ്ങുകയും കരയുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു. സഞ്ജയൻ ദുർനിമിത്തങ്ങളെക്കുറിച്ച് പറയുന്നു; മൃത്യുദേവനെപ്പോലെ ഭീഷ്മർ മഹാസേനയെ ദഹിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.108; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अथ वीरो महेष्वासो मत्तवारणविक्रमः ।\nसमादाय महच्चापं मत्तवारणवारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the heroic Drona, the great archer, who moved with the might of a rutting elephant, took up his large bow, a bow fit to check even a maddened elephant."}},{"n":2,"text":"विधुन्वानो धनुः श्रेष्ठं द्रावयाणो महारथान् ।\nपृतनां पाण्डवेयानां पातयानो महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Twanging that excellent bow, scattering the great chariot-warriors and felling the ranks of the Pandavas, that mighty warrior went on."}},{"n":3,"text":"निमित्तानि निमित्तज्ञः सर्वतो वीक्ष्य वीर्यवान् ।\nप्रतपन्तमनीकानि द्रोणः पुत्रमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Skilled in reading omens, the powerful Drona surveyed the signs on every side, and as the armies blazed with fury, he spoke to his son Ashvatthama."}},{"n":4,"text":"अयं स दिवसस्तात यत्र पार्थो महारथः ।\nजिघांसुः समरे भीष्मं परं यत्नं करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona said: \"Today, my son, is the day on which the great warrior Arjuna will make his supreme effort to kill Bhishma in battle."}},{"n":5,"text":"उत्पतन्ति हि मे बाणा धनुः प्रस्फुरतीव मे ।\nयोगमस्त्राणि गच्छन्ति क्रूरे मे वर्तते मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My arrows leap up of themselves, my bow seems to quiver, my weapons come readily to my mind, and my thoughts turn cruel."}},{"n":6,"text":"दिक्षु शान्तासु घोराणि व्याहरन्ति मृगद्विजाः ।\nनीचैर्गृध्रा निलीयन्ते भारतानां चमूं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though the quarters are calm, beasts and birds cry out dreadfully, and vultures swoop low over the Bharata host."}},{"n":7,"text":"नष्टप्रभ इवादित्यः सर्वतो लोहिता दिशः ।\nरसते व्यथते भूमिरनुष्टनति वाहनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sun seems to have lost its brightness, all the directions glow red, the earth groans and trembles, and the chariots rumble."}},{"n":8,"text":"कङ्का गृध्रा बलाकाश्च व्याहरन्ति मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nशिवाश्चाशिवनिर्घोषा वेदयन्त्यो महद्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Herons, vultures and cranes cry again and again, and jackals howl ominously, announcing a great danger."}},{"n":9,"text":"पपात महती चोल्का मध्येनादित्यमण्डलात् ।\nसकबन्धश्च परिघो भानुमावृत्य तिष्ठति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great meteor has fallen from the middle of the sun's disc, and a headless mass like an iron club hangs across the sun."}},{"n":10,"text":"परिवेषस्तथा घोरश्चन्द्रभास्करयोरभूत् ।\nवेदयानो भयं घोरं राज्ञां देहावकर्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A terrible halo has also formed around the sun and moon, foretelling the cutting down of the bodies of kings."}},{"n":11,"text":"देवतायतनस्थाश्च कौरवेन्द्रस्य देवताः ।\nकम्पन्ते च हसन्ते च नृत्यन्ति च रुदन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods in their shrines, those of the Kaurava king, shake, laugh, dance and weep."}},{"n":12,"text":"अपसव्यं ग्रहाश्चक्रुरलक्ष्माणं निशाकरम् ।\nअवाक्शिराश्च भगवानुदतिष्ठत चन्द्रमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The planets circle the moon the wrong way round, leaving it without its mark, and the revered moon has risen with its head turned downward."}},{"n":13,"text":"वपूंषि च नरेन्द्राणां विगतानीव लक्षये ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रस्य सैन्येषु न च भ्राजन्ति दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see the bodies of the kings in Dhritarashtra's armies as though drained of life, and the armored warriors do not shine."}},{"n":14,"text":"सेनयोरुभयोश्चैव समन्ताच्छ्रूयते महान् ।\nपाञ्चजन्यस्य निर्घोषो गाण्डीवस्य च निस्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On both sides the great roar of Krishna's conch Panchajanya and the twang of Arjuna's Gandiva are heard everywhere."}},{"n":15,"text":"ध्रुवमास्थाय बीभत्सुरुत्तमास्त्राणि संयुगे ।\nअपास्यान्यान्रणे योधानभ्यस्यति पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely Arjuna, taking up his finest weapons in battle, will leave aside the other warriors and attack the grandsire Bhishma."}},{"n":16,"text":"हृष्यन्ति रोमकूपानि सीदतीव च मे मनः ।\nचिन्तयित्वा महाबाहो भीष्मार्जुनसमागमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My hair stands on end and my heart sinks, mighty-armed son, as I think of the meeting of Bhishma and Arjuna."}},{"n":17,"text":"तं चैव निकृतिप्रज्ञं पाञ्चाल्यं पापचेतसम् ।\nपुरस्कृत्य रणे पार्थो भीष्मस्यायोधनं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Putting that scheming, evil-minded prince of Panchala, Shikhandi, in front, the son of Pritha has come to Bhishma's battlefield."}},{"n":18,"text":"अब्रवीच्च पुरा भीष्मो नाहं हन्यां शिखण्डिनम् ।\nस्त्री ह्येषा विहिता धात्रा दैवाच्च स पुनः पुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago Bhishma declared, 'I will not strike Shikhandi: the Creator made that one a woman, and only by fate did he become a man.'"}},{"n":19,"text":"अमङ्गल्यध्वजश्चैव याज्ञसेनिर्महारथः ।\nन चामङ्गलकेतोः स प्रहरेदापगासुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great warrior, son of Yajnasena, has an inauspicious banner, and the son of the river goddess would never strike one whose standard is of ill omen."}},{"n":20,"text":"एतद्विचिन्तयानस्य प्रज्ञा सीदति मे भृशम् ।\nअद्यैव तु रणे पार्थः कुरुवृद्धमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As I ponder this, my mind sinks deeply. Today the son of Pritha has indeed rushed upon the aged Kuru."}},{"n":21,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्य च क्रोधो भीष्मार्जुनसमागमः ।\nमम चास्त्राभिसंरम्भः प्रजानामशुभं ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira's anger, the clash of Bhishma and Arjuna, and my own fierce readiness with weapons all surely bode ill for the people."}},{"n":22,"text":"मनस्वी बलवाञ्शूरः कृतास्त्रो दृढविक्रमः ।\nदूरपाती दृढेषुश्च निमित्तज्ञश्च पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava Arjuna is high-minded, strong, brave, trained in weapons, firm in valor, a far-shooter with sturdy arrows, and reads omens well."}},{"n":23,"text":"अजेयः समरे चैव देवैरपि सवासवैः ।\nबलवान्बुद्धिमांश्चैव जितक्लेशो युधां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He cannot be conquered in battle even by the gods with Indra, for he is powerful, wise, free of weariness, and the best of warriors."}},{"n":24,"text":"विजयी च रणे नित्यं भैरवास्त्रश्च पाण्डवः ।\nतस्य मार्गं परिहरन्द्रुतं गच्छ यतव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava is always victorious in battle and wields terrible weapons. Avoid his path and go quickly, you who keep your vows."}},{"n":25,"text":"पश्य चैतन्महाबाहो वैशसं समुपस्थितम् ।\nहेमचित्राणि शूराणां महान्ति च शुभानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, mighty-armed one, at the slaughter that has arrived: the great, splendid, gold-adorned armor of heroes is being torn apart."}},{"n":26,"text":"कवचान्यवदीर्यन्ते शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nछिद्यन्ते च ध्वजाग्राणि तोमराणि धनूंषि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arrows with smooth joints split the armor; banner tops, javelins and bows are cut down."}},{"n":27,"text":"प्रासाश्च विमलास्तीक्ष्णाः शक्त्यश्च कनकोज्ज्वलाः ।\nवैजयन्त्यश्च नागानां संक्रुद्धेन किरीटिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bright sharp lances and gold-gleaming spears, and the standards on the elephants, are cut apart by the enraged wearer of the diadem, Arjuna."}},{"n":28,"text":"नायं संरक्षितुं कालः प्राणान्पुत्रोपजीविभिः ।\nयाहि स्वर्गं पुरस्कृत्य यशसे विजयाय च ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is no time for those who live by their sons' favor to guard their lives. Go to heaven, putting fame and victory first."}},{"n":29,"text":"हयनागरथावर्तां महाघोरां सुदुस्तराम् ।\nरथेन संग्रामनदीं तरत्येष कपिध्वजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This ape-bannered warrior crosses the river of battle in his chariot, a river whose whirlpools are horses, elephants and chariots, terrible and hard to cross."}},{"n":30,"text":"ब्रह्मण्यता दमो दानं तपश्च चरितं महत् ।\nइहैव दृश्यते राज्ञो भ्राता यस्य धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devotion to brahmins, self-control, charity and great austerity are all seen right here in the king whose brother is Arjuna."}},{"n":31,"text":"भीमसेनश्च बलवान्माद्रीपुत्रौ च पाण्डवौ ।\nवासुदेवश्च वार्ष्णेयो यस्य नाथो व्यवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty Bhima, the two sons of Madri, and Vasudeva of the Vrishni line stand as protectors of that king."}},{"n":32,"text":"तस्यैष मन्युप्रभवो धार्तराष्ट्रस्य दुर्मतेः ।\nतपोदग्धशरीरस्य कोपो दहति भारतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Born of Yudhishthira's wrath, the fury of the evil-minded Dhritarashtra's son, whose body is already scorched by austerity, burns the Bharatas."}},{"n":33,"text":"एष संदृश्यते पार्थो वासुदेवव्यपाश्रयः ।\nदारयन्सर्वसैन्यानि धार्तराष्ट्राणि सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is Arjuna, who has taken refuge in Vasudeva, tearing apart all the armies of Dhritarashtra's sons on every side."}},{"n":34,"text":"एतदालोक्यते सैन्यं क्षोभ्यमाणं किरीटिना ।\nमहोर्मिनद्धं सुमहत्तिमिनेव नदीमुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See how that army is being churned by Arjuna, like the mouth of a river heaving with huge waves, stirred by a great whale."}},{"n":35,"text":"हाहाकिलकिलाशब्दाः श्रूयन्ते च चमूमुखे ।\nयाहि पाञ्चालदायादमहं यास्ये युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cries of 'Alas!' and roars are heard at the front of the army. Go to the heir of Panchala; I shall go to Yudhishthira."}},{"n":36,"text":"दुर्लभं ह्यन्तरं राज्ञो व्यूहस्यामिततेजसः ।\nसमुद्रकुक्षिप्रतिमं सर्वतोऽतिरथैः स्थितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king's army formation of boundless power is hard to penetrate, like the belly of the ocean, with great chariot-warriors standing all around."}},{"n":37,"text":"सात्यकिश्चाभिमन्युश्च धृष्टद्युम्नवृकोदरौ ।\nपरिरक्षन्ति राजानं यमौ च मनुजेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, Abhimanyu, Dhrishtadyumna and Bhima guard the king, and so do the twins, protectors of men."}},{"n":38,"text":"उपेन्द्रसदृशः श्यामो महाशाल इवोद्गतः ।\nएष गच्छत्यनीकानि द्वितीय इव फल्गुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he goes among the armies, dark like Upendra, tall as a risen sala tree, like a second Arjuna."}},{"n":39,"text":"उत्तमास्त्राणि चादत्स्व गृहीत्वान्यन्महद्धनुः ।\nपार्श्वतो याहि राजानं युध्यस्व च वृकोदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Take up your finest weapons and another great bow, go to the king's side, and fight Bhima."}},{"n":40,"text":"को हि नेच्छेत्प्रियं पुत्रं जीवन्तं शाश्वतीः समाः ।\nक्षत्रधर्मं पुरस्कृत्य ततस्त्वा विनियुज्महे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who would not want a dear son to live for endless years? Yet keeping the warrior's duty before us, we send you into this."}},{"n":41,"text":"एष चापि रणे भीष्मो दहते वै महाचमूम् ।\nयुद्धे सुसदृशस्तात यमस्य वरुणस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"And here too Bhishma burns the great army in battle, in war he is quite like Yama and Varuna.\""}}]}]}